{
 "$comment": "Per-unit runs: the editor's quote of a whole run must equal the server's charge. Each case is a graph whose node `x` is priced per unit; `rateId` + `units` are what the editor prices it at, `quoteId` the id of the whole run's price (`<rateId>:<units>u`), `credits` what the server charges for it at the `pricing` block (the row's base \u00d7 the units, rounded up, marked up ONCE), `servedUnit` the one-unit price the server serves, and `perUnitQuote` the old rule (servedUnit \u00d7 whole units), which quotes more. The margins are test values, not any instance's; the per-service ones make the LTX rows round. `repeat` builds a string of that many copies of `of`.",
